# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Frontend environment variables
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# LOCAL DEVELOPMENT
#   Leave VITE_API_URL unset (comment it out).
#   The Vite dev-server proxy in vite.config.ts forwards /api/* to
#   http://localhost:8000 automatically — no variable needed.
#
# PRODUCTION (Vercel)
#   Set VITE_API_URL to your Render BACKEND URL in the Vercel dashboard:
#     Vercel → Project → Settings → Environment Variables
#
#   ⚠️  This MUST be your Render service URL — NOT your Vercel URL.
#       Your Vercel URL is the frontend.  Your Render URL is the backend.
#
#   Example (replace with YOUR actual Render URL):
#     VITE_API_URL=https://clinical-trial-api.onrender.com
#
#   How to find your Render URL:
#     Render dashboard → your Web Service → top of the page shows the URL
#     It looks like: https://<your-service-name>.onrender.com
#
# VITE_API_URL=https://your-render-service.onrender.com
